{
  "version": 1,
  "jobs": [
    {
      "id": "t5-run-record",
      "agent": "codex",
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "tier": "expensive",
      "tierReason": "merge-gate trust source and runner record; Opus review in train 5",
      "sensitive": true,
      "prompt": "FILE ACCESS: declared outputs are readable and writable. Tests first.\n\nTrain 5 correction: the review run record must be written by the swarm run/job itself, not typed into the branch by a person, and gate v2 must check the run's own state ON THIS MACHINE (the review now runs on this MacBook). A committed record that anyone can type is not acceptable.\n\nPart A - runner writes the record. In tools/swarm.mjs (the run/job completion path), when a job completes successfully and its outputs include a path matching `coordination/review/<name>-review.json` (but not `-review-run.json`), write `.swarm/runs/<runId>/review-record.json` from the runner (never the worker) with:\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"runId\": \"<state.id>\",\n  \"jobId\": \"<job.id>\",\n  \"agent\": \"<job.agent>\",\n  \"model\": \"<job.model or actualModel>\",\n  \"manifest\": \".swarm/runs/<runId>/manifest.json\",\n  \"head\": \"<state.baseCommit>\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"resultFile\": \"<the declared output path>\",\n  \"resultHash\": \"<sha256 of the result file bytes in the job workspace>\",\n  \"finishedAt\": \"<job.finishedAt>\",\n  \"stateFile\": \".swarm/runs/<runId>/state.json\"\n}\nWrite it atomically with the same helper style as other state writes; if the result file or hash cannot be read, write nothing and log a fixed warning (do not fail the run). Add a focused test that builds a temp run dir + workspace with a review output and asserts the record fields/hash; and a non-review output writes no record.\n\nPart B - gate v2 checks the local run. In tools/merge-guard.mjs replace the committed-GitHub-record verification with:\n1) The PR body carries only a selector line `<!-- swarm-review: <review manifest path> -->` (e.g. coordination/manifests/review-train5.json). No typed verdict/record is trusted.\n2) In the local repo at the merge root, read `.swarm/runs/*/review-record.json` and find a record with `head === headRefOid`, `manifest === <selector>`, `agent === 'claude'`, `/opus/i.test(model)`, `status === 'complete'`, and a matching run state file that is `status === 'complete'`, `state.baseCommit === headRefOid`, and whose job with the record.jobId is complete with the same agent/model. Refuse if none (distinct reasons: review-run-record-missing, review-run-state-mismatch, review-run-model-not-opus).\n3) The review result commit R: fetch from GitHub at the PR head the commit's parents and the compare R^...R. Require exactly one parent H equal to the record.head; the compare touches ONLY the record.resultFile. Fetch the result file bytes at R and require sha256 == record.resultHash; parse the JSON: verdict exactly 'pass' and, if `head` is present, it equals H. Refuse on any mismatch (result-hash-mismatch, result-verdict, result-head-mismatch, result-not-metadata-commit).\n4) The gate runs before any gh pr merge. Non-release PRs exempt. Remove the old committed-review-run.json and free JSON block trust paths from the gate.\n\nTests (tests/merge-guard.test.mjs): fake the local `.swarm/runs` directory (pass a root with records/state) and fake gh contents/commits/compare. Cases: a matching local record + metadata-only result commit + pass result -> merged; no local record but a typed committed record or JSON block -> refused; local model not opus -> refused; state baseCommit != head -> refused; result commit touching code -> refused; result hash/verdict/head mismatch -> refused; non-release PR -> merged; a fence-aware selector inside a fenced block does not count; null body refuses. Keep the mechanical runMerge tests green. Add the selector to the train 5 PR body separately (not in this job).\n\nVerify: node --import ./tests/_isolate-config.mjs --test tests/merge-guard.test.mjs tests/review-record.test.mjs tests/guard-backup-fixes.test.mjs tests/guard-backup-fixes4.test.mjs tests/state-guard.test.mjs -> all pass. Report counts.",
      "context": [
        "tools/merge-guard.mjs",
        "tests/merge-guard.test.mjs"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "tools/swarm.mjs",
        "tools/merge-guard.mjs",
        "tests/merge-guard.test.mjs",
        "tests/review-record.test.mjs"
      ],
